  "narrative": "No claim is currently supported by the accumulated evidence as a clinically meaningful predictor or subgroup association in this dataset. The due validations show that the strongest candidate did not replicate. H34 tested outcome_006 with feature_002=1 versus 0 within feature_034=0 under the stronger-dependency hypothesis. Discovery R27 gave signed effect +0.0395, about 22.5% of the absolute outcome_006 mean and well above the 10% threshold of about 0.0175, but independent validation R39 gave only +0.0072, about 4.1%, with interval [-0.0696, +0.0839]. The validation point estimate is below the clinical threshold, includes the null, and is inconsistent with the discovery magnitude. I therefore do not accept H34. I keep it unresolved but closed because the wide intervals still cannot formally exclude a clinically meaningful positive effect, while concluding that this subgroup localization is not a useful lead. This also weakens, but does not by itself kill, H13, the population outcome_006/feature_002 claim. H13 remains active because it is the only direct claim with a discovery point estimate above the threshold: R2 is +0.0209, about 11.9%, interval [-0.0139, +0.0556]. The subgroup failure suggests caution, but a population-level association could still replicate even if the feature_034=0 localization failed. H7 outcome_002/feature_050 validation R13 gives signed effect +0.0044, about 1.7%, after discovery R7 +0.0151, about 5.8%; both intervals include the null, and the validation upper bound remains above threshold. I keep H7 unresolved but closed: there is no support for a clinically meaningful effect, but absolute exclusion is not possible. H15 outcome_009/feature_042 was previously rejected because the discovery estimate was near null/opposite and its upper bound was below threshold. New validation R40 is also near null, signed +0.0019, about 0.7%, but its wide independent interval upper bound +0.0290 slightly crosses the threshold of about 0.0256. To remain consistent with uncertainty, I change H15 from reject to unresolved but closed; this is not support, only a refusal to claim absolute exclusion under the very wide validation interval. The overall pattern across H30, H7, H15, and H34 is that borderline discovery associations do not replicate. Earlier negative findings remain informative: many population screens were rejected because their direction-aligned upper bounds fell below the 10% threshold, and the feature_021/outcome_005 line is deprioritized after the failed H30 validation and weak H39 complement result. I therefore close H14 as unresolved but low yield. Secondary unresolved leads are H35 outcome_006/feature_008, H37 outcome_014/feature_064, and H45 outcome_014/feature_050, but each has wide uncertainty and multiplicity concerns. The most informative next analysis is validation of H13, the population outcome_006/feature_002 stronger-dependency claim. If validation yields an interval that excludes null and the point estimate remains above about 0.0175, that would support a dataset-specific population association; if validation is near null, opposite, or imprecise, the outcome_006/feature_002 line should be closed. In parallel, analysis should prioritize the untested high-prevalence coverage screens H46, H47, H48, H49, H50, H51, and H52, with lower-prevalence H20-H26 used only if capacity remains. All statements remain dataset-specific, associational, and noncausal; predictor labels are opaque, and multiple testing limits confidence.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 3 synthesis: no accepted claims. Validations: H7 R13 +0.0044 vs threshold 0.0260 after discovery 0.0151; H15 R40 +0.0019 vs threshold 0.0256, upper 0.0290, so downgraded to unresolved closed; H34 R39 +0.0072 vs threshold 0.0175 after discovery 0.0395, subgroup failed, unresolved closed. H13 remains active as main validation candidate: population outcome_006/feature_002 direction -1, R2 +0.0209 interval [-0.0139,+0.0556], threshold 0.0175. If H13 validates positive and interval excludes null, accept dataset-specific; otherwise close outcome_006/feature_002 line. H30/H39 feature_021 failed or weak; H14 closed unresolved. Secondary deferred: H35 +0.0178 threshold 0.0175 wide; H37 +0.0122 threshold 0.0093 wide; H45 +0.0122 threshold 0.0093 wide. New high-prevalence proposals H49 outcome_005/feature_030, H50 outcome_013/feature_030, H51 outcome_015/feature_008, H52 outcome_014/feature_002. Existing active high-prevalence: H46 outcome_007/feature_023, H47 outcome_016/feature_030, H48 outcome_012/feature_023. Prioritize these in analyze. Keep findings noncausal and dataset-specific; multiplicity especially outcome_014."
