on.\n\nMost informative next analysis: continue processing the already registered active broad-coverage panels, especially the feature_042 and feature_045 panels and other untested binary/categorical comparisons, while avoiding opportunistic validation of weak or reverse-derived signals. A future candidate should only be considered after consistent same-predictor/outcome evidence near or above the outcome-specific 10% threshold, preferably supported by adjacent outcome panels with similar direction and magnitude. All claims remain dataset-specific associations; no causal interpretation or generalizability is supported.",
