ter focused or independent testing: feature_008/outcome_008 collapsed in validation; the feature_021/feature_034 subgroup lead was not replicated; the feature_048 panel lacked cross-outcome consistency; the feature_019 panel had one wide-interval threshold-exceeding point but otherwise discordant or subthreshold results. These patterns are more consistent with screening noise, outcome correlation, rare-category instability, and limited replication power than with robust predictor effects.\n\nRemaining uncertainty is mostly due to imprecision around rare levels and subgroup analyses, multiple correlated outcomes, and the opaque predictor labels. The evidence supports dataset-specific association assessments only; it does not support causal claims or generalizability beyond this supplied dataset. The most informative next step is to continue processing the already registered broad-coverage deferred panels, especially feature_042, feature_045, and other untested binary/categorical contrasts, while applying a higher bar before validation: only consider a candidate if it is near or above its outcome-specific threshold with supportive uncertainty, or if the same predictor contrast shows a coherent pattern across adjacent outcomes. Further validation should not be spent on single borderline point estimates, reverse-derived claims, or inconsistent panels.",
