ction and complement tests H192 through H196, especially H192 and H196, to test whether the secondary conditional effects represent clinically meaningful effect modification or remain below threshold. These should be evaluated as associations in the supplied dataset only, not as causal or generalizable effects. Multiplicity and correlated predictor structure make secondary claims vulnerable, while the dominant feature_021 effect is large enough that multiplicity is unlikely but causal interpretation still requires external evidence.",
