 "narrative": "I assessed all newly delivered results under the same operational 10 percent rule used earlier: a clinically meaningful absolute mean difference is approximately 0.10 times the absolute overall outcome mean. For the outcomes examined here this is about 0.0256 for outcome_009, 0.0250 for outcome_015, 0.0250 for outcome_005, 0.0175 for outcome_006, and 0.0093 for outcome_014. All estimates and intervals were already signed to the registered hypothesis direction, and I did not multiply them again. The central conclusion remains unchanged: the only decisive, independently validated association is the very large feature_021 versus feature_021=0 effect on outcome_006 (H146); accepted stratum claims are coherent expressions of that same dataset-specific effect, not independent predictors.\n\nThe new conditional analyses did not produce a new clinically established association. H192 (outcome_009 feature_048 level_003 versus level_001, interaction by feature_019 level_002) has signed estimate +0.0283, with CI -0.0113 to +0.0680. The point estimate is near the outcome_009 threshold, but the interval includes both null and sub-threshold effects, and the interaction cells are smaller. This is not sufficient to claim effect modification, so I close it unresolved. H193 and H194 test whether the feature_065 contrast on outcome_015 is modified by, or present within, feature_021=1. H193 signed estimate is -0.0294, which is opposite the claimed negative interaction, and H194 in feature_021=1 is essentially null (signed -0.0023, wide interval). Together with R154 in feature_021=0, this pattern suggests the feature_065 signal, if real, is concentrated outside feature_021=1. I reject the negative interaction claim and the feature_021=1 association claim, while keeping H200 as a separate unresolved localization result. H195 (outcome_014 feature_065 interaction by feature_021=1) is positive in the claimed direction (+0.0579) but very imprecise and includes null; small conditional cells and multiplicity make acceptance inappropriate. H196 (outcome_005 feature_021 interaction by feature_019 level_002) has signed estimate +0.0165, below threshold and with CI crossing null, so I reject evidence of clinically meaningful modification. H197 tests whether feature_065 modifies the dominant feature_021 effect on outcome_006; the interaction is near zero (-0.0037), although the interval is wide. This provides no support for meaningful modification, though it does not prove absence because the interval includes large effects. I reject the modification claim as unsupported.\n\nThe most clinically relevant secondary signals are H198 and H200. H198 (outcome_009 feature_048 level_003 versus level_001 within feature_021=0) has signed estimate +0.0257, lower bound +0.0037. This excludes null but the lower bound is far below the threshold, so the data support a non-zero association but not a clinically established 10 percent effect. I keep it unresolved and close active follow-up on it. H200 (outcome_015 feature_065 within feature_019 level_002 and feature_021=0) has signed estimate +0.0326 with lower bound +0.0048. The point estimate exceeds threshold, but uncertainty includes substantial sub-threshold effects, so I do not accept it; it remains unresolved and is localized enough to merit one targeted interaction proposal. H199, within feature_021=0 on outcome_015, is below threshold and imprecise; I reject it. H201 is a very small, non-significant outcome_014 double-subgroup estimate; I reject it. H202 is positive but extremely wide (CI -0.0461 to +0.0755), and conditioning on higher log-PFS adds selection/collider concerns; I close it unresolved rather than accept. H204 is a broad screen with a near-zero signed estimate; I reject it.\n\nMethodologically, the dominant feature_021/outcome_006 effect is so large that multiplicity is unlikely to explain it, but it could still be a technical or population-structure axis rather than a causal or generalizabl