  "narrative": "No assessments are due. The dominant validated finding remains the very large feature_021=1 versus feature_021=0 contrast on outcome_006; the registered active tests H205, H206, and H207 should be interpreted as localization/interaction checks around the only two residual threshold-adjacent secondary candidates: H198 for outcome_009 feature_048 and H200 for outcome_015 feature_065. The new proposals are designed to decide whether either candidate is a genuinely secondary association crossing an approximately 10 percent absolute-outcome-mean threshold, or merely a near-null signal localized by correlated feature_021/feature_019 structure.\n\nFor outcome_009 feature_048 level_003 versus level_001, the claimed direction is negative because prior estimates are consistent with raw level_003 scores being more negative than level_001, i.e. stronger dependency. The operational threshold is about 0.0256. Proposal 1 asks whether this contrast remains clinically relevant in the feature_021=0 population when further restricted to feature_019 level_002. Proposal 2 asks whether it remains relevant in feature_021=1 within feature_019 level_002. Proposal 3 asks whether a comparable contrast appears in feature_019 level_001 within feature_021=0, using level_001 as a practical proxy for the non-level_002 complement. Proposal 4 tests, among feature_021=0 observations, whether the level_003-minus-level_001 contrast is stronger in feature_019 level_002 than in its complement. The expected raw interaction is negative if feature_019 level_002 is the biologically relevant localizing stratum. Plausible alternatives are a null interaction if the feature_048 association is broad, an opposite interaction if level_002 attenuates the effect, or a null main contrast if the earlier H198 signal was driven by correlated feature_021 structure or post-selection.\n\nFor outcome_015 feature_065, the operational threshold is about 0.0250. Proposal 5 tests the complement of H200: feature_065=1 versus 0 within feature_019 level_002 but in the feature_021=1 population. If the H200 signal is genuinely tied to the feature_021=0 stratum, this comparison should be near null or opposite to the claimed negative direction. Proposal 6 tests whether the same feature_065 contrast appears in feature_019 level_001 within feature_021=0, using level_001 as a proxy for the non-level_002 complement. Proposal 7 tests the feature_019 level_002 interaction for feature_065 in the full population, which is more powerful than H207's feature_021=0 eligibility but may be diluted if feature_021=1 is null. The expected raw direction for feature_065 is negative in strata where dependency is stronger, but the anticipated raw direction is deliberately left uncertain for complement tests because localization is the scientific question. If any of these comparisons yields a signed lower bound above approximately 0.0250 for outcome_015 or 0.0256 for outcome_009, it would be eligible for acceptance; if it only excludes null but has a lower bound below that threshold, it should remain unresolved or be closed rather than accepted.\n\nNo independent validation is requested at this explore stage. H146 is already validated, while the secondary candidates are threshold-adjacent and have discovery intervals whose lower bounds fall below the 10 percent threshold; validation intervals are wider and may not resolve threshold crossing unless the underlying effect is much larger. All results will be interpreted as dataset-specific associations, not causal effects or externally generalizable claims.",
