  "narrative": "I assessed all newly delivered discovery results using the same operational 10 percent clinical-significance rule used previously: a mean difference is treated as clinically meaningful only when the signed point estimate is clearly above roughly one tenth of the absolute overall outcome mean and the confidence interval supports that threshold. For the outcomes in this batch the approximate thresholds are about 0.0256 for outcome_009, 0.0250 for outcome_015, 0.0415 for outcome_001, 0.0282 for outcome_008, and 0.0301 for outcome_011. All returned estimates and intervals are already signed to the registered hypothesis direction and were not re-signed. No new claim was accepted. The accepted evidence set therefore remains unchanged, with H146 still the only decisive, independently validated association: feature_021 equals 1 versus 0 has a very large positive mean_difference on outcome_006. The new results were mainly localization, stratum, and interaction checks around secondary candidates, and they do not establish a new clinically meaningful association.\n\nFor outcome_009 feature_048 level_003 versus level_001, the signal remains threshold-adjacent but uncertain. H205, within feature_021 equals 1, has a signed estimate of about 0.0427, which is above the outcome_009 threshold, but its 95 percent interval is about -0.0036 to 0.0890. Thus it does not even exclude the null at the usual discovery level, and its lower bound is far below the clinically relevant threshold. I keep it unresolved but close it because the follow-up set has already probed the most informative strata. H206 tested whether the outcome_009 feature_048 contrast is modified by feature_021 status; the signed interaction is about -0.0170 with interval about -0.0680 to 0.0340. This gives no evidence for a clinically meaningful positive interaction and is not worth further pursuit, so I reject it. H208 tests the contrast within feature_021 equals 0 and feature_019 level_002 and has signed 