nant feature_021-outcome_006 axis, not as independent secondary predictors.\n\nNegative or unsupported lines include the H261 feature_057 interaction just closed, the previously closed feature_048-outcome_009 subgroup line validated in H240 (R209 failed replication), and the broad set of secondary mean differences and interaction screens that either had point estimates below the clinical threshold or confidence intervals incompatible with a robust clinically meaningful effect. In particular, most interaction heterogeneity claims for the central outcome remain unsupported; several were closed unresolved because they were too imprecise to establish or rule out heterogeneity, but none cleared the independent-lower-bound rule.\n\nRemaining uncertainty is mainly at the margins: some secondary outcome_014, outcome_015, outcome_009, and outcome_005 associations are threshold-adjacent or imprecise, and some interactions cannot be completely ruled out. However, these are lower-priority relative to the central finding and should not drive further exploratory subgroup mining unless a pre-specified biological or clinical rationale emerges. The most informative next analysis is not another broad subgroup sweep but targeted replication or mechanistic follow-up of the dominant feature_021-outcome_006 axis: an independent external cohort with pre-specified estimation of the feature_021 contrast, preferably with covariate adjustment or a model-based robustness check, and biological interpretation of why feature_021=1 is associated with much weaker outcome_006 dependency. All conclusions here remain dataset-specific associations, not causal effects or claims of generalizability."
